1258 0 obj
  << /ActualText (We are interested in something as apparently absurd as the notion of what happens when the protagonist is an internet connected toaster\077 What does it\0506\051  mean if someone\031s best friend is a very dumb comfort bot\077 Or what does it mean to tell the story of the city through the operating system of the city\077 Or what does it mean to design a city and a space for non\055human inhabitants\077 And that is leading to very novel forms of film\055making\056\nWe are in the territory of post\055cinema where the traditional genres we understand like romantic comedy\054 horror\054 drama etc\056 don\047t necessarily apply anymore\056 We are taking traditional characters out of the equation and looking for new storytelling potential that comes out of the context of this new technology\056)
     /K [ 52 ]
     /P 1259 0 R
     /Pg 1154 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

